# Development Workflow Standards

## Git Workflow

### Branch Strategy
- **main**: Production-ready code (protected)
- **develop**: Integration branch for features
- **feature/**: Feature development branches
- **hotfix/**: Critical bug fixes
- **release/**: Release preparation branches

### Branch Naming Convention
```
feature/strategy-search-optimization
hotfix/memory-leak-fix
release/v1.2.0
```

### Commit Message Standards

#### Conventional Commits Format
```
<type>[optional scope]: <description>

[optional body]

[optional footer(s)]
```

#### Types
- **feat**: New feature
- **fix**: Bug fix
- **docs**: Documentation changes
- **style**: Code style changes (formatting, etc.)
- **refactor**: Code refactoring
- **test**: Adding or updating tests
- **chore**: Maintenance tasks

#### Examples
```
feat(search): add fuzzy search capability for strategies

Implement Whoosh-based fuzzy search with relevance scoring
to improve strategy discovery for debugging scenarios.

Closes #123
```

```
fix(repository): handle git authentication timeout

Add retry logic and proper error handling for git operations
when authentication tokens expire or network issues occur.

Fixes #456
```

### Pre-commit Hooks

#### Required Checks
```yaml
# .pre-commit-config.yaml
repos:
  - repo: https://github.com/psf/black
    rev: 23.12.1
    hooks:
      - id: black
        language_version: python3.10

  - repo: https://github.com/pycqa/isort
    rev: 5.13.2
    hooks:
      - id: isort

  - repo: https://github.com/pycqa/flake8
    rev: 7.0.0
    hooks:
      - id: flake8

  - repo: https://github.com/pre-commit/mirrors-mypy
    rev: v1.8.0
    hooks:
      - id: mypy
```

## Code Review Process

### Pull Request Requirements

#### Checklist
- [ ] **Tests**: Unit tests added/updated with 90%+ coverage
- [ ] **Documentation**: Code documented with docstrings
- [ ] **Type Hints**: Full type annotations present
- [ ] **Linting**: All linting checks pass
- [ ] **Performance**: No performance regressions
- [ ] **Security**: No security vulnerabilities introduced

#### PR Template
```markdown
## Description
Brief description of changes and motivation.

## Type of Change
- [ ] Bug fix (non-breaking change)
- [ ] New feature (non-breaking change)
- [ ] Breaking change (fix or feature causing existing functionality to change)
- [ ] Documentation update

## Testing
- [ ] Unit tests pass
- [ ] Integration tests pass
- [ ] Manual testing completed

## Strategy Coverage
- [ ] New strategies added to repository
- [ ] Strategy metadata updated
- [ ] Search index updated

## Checklist
- [ ] Code follows project style guidelines
- [ ] Self-review completed
- [ ] Code commented, particularly complex areas
- [ ] Documentation updated
- [ ] No new warnings introduced
```

### Review Guidelines

#### For Authors
1. **Self-review**: Review your own PR before requesting review
2. **Small PRs**: Keep changes focused and small (<500 lines)
3. **Clear descriptions**: Explain what, why, and how
4. **Test coverage**: Ensure adequate test coverage
5. **Documentation**: Update relevant documentation

#### For Reviewers
1. **Timely reviews**: Review within 24 hours
2. **Constructive feedback**: Focus on code quality and maintainability
3. **Security focus**: Look for potential security issues
4. **Performance considerations**: Consider performance implications
5. **Test quality**: Verify test coverage and quality

